<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=5&y=2003">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=4&y=2003">April-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=3&y=2003">March-2003</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=2&y=2003">February-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=1&y=2003">January-2003</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?m=12&y=2002">December-2002</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><CENTER><font size=+2>December, 2002</font><BR></center><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>The bar is raised!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Tuesday - December 31st 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Several have mentioned how a level 40 requirement is too low for Legerd.  Personally I saw the time as a growth period. It allowed lower level members to get a feel for the guild and gain from the knowledge of others as they leveled.  Others pointed out that these lower level members have a rough time feeling like part of the clan since they're not really high enough to group, and in some cases to even raid with us.<BR>
<BR>
I tended to disagree and hung on to the level 40 requirement.  Since PoP came out, this has changed.  The move towards 65 has increased the gap even further.  As a result, I've moved the level requirement for a main to level 50.  Hopefully this will help ease newcomers in to the guild.<BR>
<BR>
Note: This does not apply to Rhandar since he applied before this change took place.  Actually applied before he met the level 40 requirement *cough* hehe. If Rhandar is still interested when he hits 40, he'll be voted on.</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>OMG! We killed Trak!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Monday - December 30th 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Can you believe it?  Almost totally Leger kill of Trak.  Once we got down, we spent a good hour fiddling with positioning and trying to clear his lair, but we eventually got it all taken care of with 28 people.<BR>
I hear that I might be getting some nice screenshots for this post hehe.  I'll be sure to insert them here when I get them for those that weren't able to attend.<BR>
Farlander ended up with the Cobalt BP and Hriyn got the Deepwater BP.  Embren, Keymarad, Ninden, Tileren, and Dakiln got the teeth.  We'll need a few more of those before we play around in VP hehe.<BR>

Very nice and fast kill everyone! Lets do it again eh?</font><BR><table align="left" width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="3"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" bgcolor="#000000">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>M.I.A.!!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" bgcolor="#000000"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - December 22nd 2002</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.jpg" cellpadding="15" border="3" bordercolor="#000000" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Have U seen these doodz?<BR>
Dinke, 52nd short drood.  Has been known to hide under horses.<BR>
Xanisx, 52nd scaled boner.  Hangs out in Felwithe terrorizing innocents.<BR>
Helmm, Kelerk, Geral.  Gruesome trio keeps quiet but strikes when you least expect it.<BR>
Lochdanan, 46th pally.  Last seen near Umbral Plains poking undead with a stick.  We fear the worst.<BR>
Oadana, 51st veterinarian. Her distant relative, Careny, has recently resurfaced after a long sabbatical.  It has been rumored that Careny has secretly done away with Oadana and stolen her identity for money and power.<BR>
Roldanious, 60th finger wagler. Rumors have been spreading that the voice of this mysterious soul can be heard echoing throughout Norrath.<BR>
Skrambold, 60th cook.  Specializes in breakfast dishes.  We suspect that somewhere.. out there.. he's fallen and can't get up.<BR>
<BR>
Each of them should be considered heavily armed and smell dangerous.  If you spot any of them, please do NOT approach them! For your own nasal safety, we urge you to contact your nearest authority figure and take a screenshot.<BR>
We thank you for your cooperation :>
